WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.680
It's been 16 years since Keanu Reeves put
down his leather duster and sunglasses as

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.880
he walked away from his role as Neo in The
Matrix trilogy.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.040
But now that he's returning to the familiar
dystopian universe to become "The One" once

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.780
again in The Matrix 4, he's sharing his thoughts
on the new film.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.940
Chatting with Entertainment Tonight, Reeves
spoke up about the script for the fourth Matrix

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.220
film, which was officially announced in August
2019.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.680
As Reeves walked the red carpet for Semper
Fi, the upcoming British drama film produced

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.520
by his sister Karina Miller, he told ET that
he'd read the script for The Matrix 4.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.500
"Are you happy about where Neo is at?

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.520
"Yeah, no, absolutely. It's very ambitious as it should be!"

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.800
Admittedly, there isn't a lot to go on with
Reeves' comments, but it's still thrilling

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.520
to hear that he's getting pumped up about
returning to one of his many career-defining

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.360
roles.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.420
Plus, "ambitious" is definitely an interesting
word considering that the original Matrix

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:02.430
trilogy changed the sci-fi movie genre, ultimately
defining an entire era of action sequences,

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.280
special effects, and world-building.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.440
Thought very little is known about The Matrix
4 yet, we do know that the film is set to

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:13.540
push even more boundaries and deliver insightful,
incisive, and interesting commentary on our

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.720
current society.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.420
As Lana Wachowski noted when announcing The
Matrix 4, the ideas that she and her sister

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:23.740
Lilly explored 20 years ago with the first
film are even more relevant now.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:29.200
When the first Matrix film hit theaters in
1999, audiences were blown away by the extraordinarily

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.040
intricate world which presented a reality
that wasn't actually real.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.180
The world everyone thought they were living
in was revealed to be a computer simulation

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:42.220
created by machines that humans tried to overpower;
everything in this fake "reality" is created

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.220
for humans by those computers.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:49.040
When he's given the chance to escape the Matrix
and learn the truth, Neo sees the dark real

00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:53.270
world where the sun is blotted out and humans
must survive by hiding from the machines both

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.060
inside and outside of the Matrix itself.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.659
In the end, it turns out Neo is "The One,"
a fated hero who can actually control the

00:02:00.659 --> 00:02:05.070
Matrix while within the simulation, thereby
being the only person who has any hope of

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.050
stopping the machines in their tracks.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:11.760
After The Matrix: Reloaded was released in
2003, the trilogy seemed like it came to a

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.180
definitive end with The Matrix: Revolutions,
which hit theaters later that same year.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:21.590
At the conclusion of Revolutions, Neo sacrifices
himself to save humanity and bring an end

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.420
to the human and machine conflict.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:28.220
With a conclusion that final, it seems strange
that Reeves could possibly return for a fourth

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:29.020
installment.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:34.180
But we know that both Reeves and Carrie Anne-Moss
are firmly aboard The Matrix 4 and will reprise

00:02:34.189 --> 00:02:38.420
their roles as characters who were last seen
dying, so clearly the minds behind the new

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.140
film found a way to resurrect Neo and Trinity.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:44.620
Reeves has certainly kept busy in the years
since he last played Neo.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.950
After appearing in various romantic comedies
as well as Richard Linklater's adaptation

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:54.019
of A Scanner Darkly, he produced a documentary
entitled Side by Side and earned his first

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.740
directing credit on the underrated Man of
Tai Chi.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:01.640
However, thanks to two stuntmen from the original
Matrix films, Reeves returned to his action

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:05.969
roots in 2014 with John Wick, which ended
up becoming its own trilogy.

00:03:05.969 --> 00:03:10.519
Alongside these butt-kicking projects, Reeves
has taken the time to appear in some comedic

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:11.680
projects as well.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.159
He starred in Destination Wedding and made
self-parodying cameos in the Netflix original

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:19.560
films Always Be My Maybe and Between Two Ferns:
The Movie.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.939
He may have bounced around genres since the
Matrix trilogy wrapped, but Reeves has planted

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:27.720
himself firmly in the pop culture canon with
his recent film appearances.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.500
There's truly no better time than now for
a Reeves-led Matrix 4, and we can't wait to

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.540
see what it's like.

